A||||10||Pontiaddict||Anyone with an 86 v6 4spd, A little help here. >||||1||
Z||000000||Pontiaddict||07-03-2000||11:09 PM||||If anyone happens to look at the wiring harness by the speed sensor on the tranny, could you please tell me what the other wire on that part of the harness is connected to?<P>It is a 2 prong plug (male end) with a blue wire and a green wire (possibly with a white tracer) and it is the only other wire on that  part of the harness. I can't find where the thing plugs into. It doesn't show it in the worthless haynes manual either.<P>Thanks for the help.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fret Naught||07-03-2000||11:25 PM||||Well if it is any consiliation, I have the same thing, and no idea where it plugs in at,either. ||||reg||10
Z||000002||Oreif||07-04-2000||01:44 AM||||It's a connector for the automatic trans. My first 86 SE was a 4spd and I saw the connector. Traced out wires and it's for the auto trans. They used 1 harness for both set-ups. If memory serves me correctly it's the electrical connector for the converter lock-up solinoid on the trans. <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 07-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||07-04-2000||02:10 AM||||I have an 88 Coupe with an engine from my old 86SE and with it came all the wiring. The 2.8 used to be mated to a 4 speed but now is bolted to a 5 speed Isuzu. The 4 speed had the reverse switch in the shifter and the Isuzu has it inside the tranny. I plugged that into the Isuzu tranny (the 5 speed shifter doesn't have the lever for the reverse lights in it and the 4 speed shifter won't work with the 5 speed tranny) and my reverse lights work. I don't know exactly what it's for, but it will work on the reverse lights.<P>P.S. when that engine/wiring was in my 86 it wasn't plugged into anything.<P>------------------<BR>-Chris <BR>88 Fiero Coupe<BR>V6 Fastback<p>[This message has been edited by SCCA FIERO (edited 07-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT Bastard||07-04-2000||02:20 AM||||It's you're speed sensor.||||reg||1
Z||000005||stimpy||07-04-2000||10:50 AM||||I agree with Oreif (Circle gets the square!) ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fret Naught||07-04-2000||12:42 PM||||Now those are the kind of answers That go right along with my motto, if it ain't broke, don't fix it.<BR>Thanks guys, your the best||||reg||10
Z||000007||TheFiero64||07-04-2000||12:52 PM||||It is the plug for the backup lights if you had a 5 speed. if you connect the 2 ends with a paperclip your backup lights turn on. I use this connection on my 88 with an isuzu 5 speed and a V6 engine.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BU.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by TheFiero64 (edited 07-04-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000008||Pontiaddict||07-04-2000||01:26 PM||||SCCA, 64, I was just thinking about that being the backup light switch wiring. <P>Oreif, they could have possibly used the same wiring for the auto too.<P>GT The speed sensor was already plugged in so I knew it wasn't it.<P>Thanks!||||reg||14
Z||000009||wxxo||07-06-2000||04:15 PM||||ive got that same loose wire and was thinking that it was the backup light too. mine do not work and that was not plugged in and had no place for it to plug into. as far as backup lights go... what could be the problem?? ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Taijiguy||07-07-2000||05:45 PM||||If you've got the four speed, the reverse light switch is up next to the shifter, under the console. The switch may need adjusted or replaced. I've been fighting with mine forever it seems. I can't seem to get it to adjust so that they actually come on with the car in reverse, that they don't come on every time I downshift. Frustrating piece of engineering in there....||||reg||1
